[0.0, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Pointer-guided ferrofluid spikes in wild fauvist orange and violet, flickering through zoetrope frames as\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m  magnets pull, a 10 second looping animation in three.js, as a single web page.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[116.676, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mWrote 1 file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Write(<workspace>/ferrofluid-zoetrope.html)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[126.122, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I built the animation as a single page: `<workspace>/ferrofluid-zoetrope.html`. Open it in a browser; it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  loads three.js from a CDN. I haven't run it in a browser, so the shaders haven't been checked on a real GPU.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What you'll see**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **The ferrofluid:** a round dish of fluid whose surface rises into a hexagonal grid of spikes, the pattern\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  real ferrofluid forms under a magnet. Spikes only grow where the magnetic field is strong enough. They lean\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  toward the nearest magnet and come and go as the magnets move.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **The magnets:** three glowing rings hover above the dish, each with a thin line down to the surface. Two\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  orbit on fixed paths, and their strength surges four times per loop, so the spikes repeatedly jump up and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  relax.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Pointer guidance:** the brightest ring follows your mouse or finger and pulls hardest. If you stop\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  moving for 2.5 seconds, it drifts back onto an automatic figure-eight path.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Fauvist colour:** the shading is split into flat bands running from deep violet through electric violet\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and hot magenta to cadmium orange and butter yellow. Edges get the opposite colour as a rim (orange on\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  violet, violet on orange). There are also hard white highlights and brush-like streaks that change every\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  frame.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Zoetrope effect:** the picture updates only 12 times a second, so motion steps instead of gliding. Each\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  frame also gets:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - dark vertical slits that shift sideways a notch,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - a slight brightness flicker and a small camera jitter, like an old projector,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - a bright orange flash on each magnet surge.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    A frame counter in the corner reads \"frame 001 / 120\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The 10-second loop:** everything is driven by a frame number from 0 to 119, and every orbit, surge and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  camera sway completes a whole number of cycles in that time. The loop is seamless, apart from the pointer-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  controlled magnet, which follows you instead of the clock.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I can also publish it as a private claude.ai page if you want a link to share.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
