[940.006, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ Chrome and Node are already on this machine, so the only extra thing I need is `puppeteer-core`, installed\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  into `.ambition/`, to drive Chrome headlessly. I won't ask about access. Here is the task restated:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  You asked for:   Pointer-guided ferrofluid spikes in wild fauvist orange and violet, flickering through\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   zoetrope frames as magnets pull, a 10 second looping animation in three.js, as a single web\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  page.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Raises all of:   • Ferrofluid spikes: a glossy black fluid with mirror-like reflections. Spikes rise in a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  hexagonal\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                     pattern, crowd around and merge toward each magnet, collapse back into the pool and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  wobble\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                     after being disturbed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • Pointer-guided: the pointer is the strongest magnet, so the fluid visibly follows and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  tears\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                     toward it. Touch works the same way. It's obvious without instructions.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • Wild fauvist orange and violet: colour treated like Matisse or Derain treated it. It is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                     structural and non-naturalistic, warm against cool, with complementary shadows, and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                     colour drives the forms instead of decorating them.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • Zoetrope frames: the stepped, strobed frames read as a real optical toy with slits, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  drum and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                     per-frame variation. The stepping looks deliberate, never laggy.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • Magnets pull: each surge has a readable rhythm of anticipation, a snap and a relaxing\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  settle.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • 10 s loop: frame-exact and seamless.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • three.js, one web page: still one self-contained HTML file.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Genre bar:       Generative-art and creative-coding showcases are judged on whether the first second stops\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   the scroll, whether the motion feels alive rather than procedural, whether it holds up as a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   framed still, whether the interaction is satisfying within seconds, and whether a second\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  look\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   reveals hidden intent such as art-historical references, compositional geometry and a loop\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  that\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   tells a small story. People pick a piece like this over the alternatives when it couldn't\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   plausibly be a stock shader.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Aiming at:       A portfolio showpiece that makes viewers feel \"a human couldn't have hand-built this in an\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   afternoon\". It should be technically uncanny and artistically literate, with layers that\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   reward a second and third look. That's the goal you described.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Excellent means: • It reads as liquid, not geometry, at first glance.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • Every one of the 120 frames would hold up as a fauvist still.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • A steady 60 fps on desktop at 1× and 2× pixel density, holding up under a 4× CPU-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  throttled run.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • Frame 0 and frame 120 render pixel-identical with the pointer idle.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • Pointer response appears within one zoetrope frame.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • An optional reveal shows the technique, such as the magnetic field lines or the zoetrope\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  drum.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • At least two deliberate hidden layers of artistic meaning that are discoverable but not\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                     announced.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • Worse than the first version on nothing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Proven by:       • Headless Chrome contact sheets of 12 frames across the loop at desktop and phone sizes,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                     side by side with .ambition/first.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • Chrome performance traces showing frame times at normal speed and 4× CPU throttle.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • A pixel diff of the first and last loop frames.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m                   • Your review of the rendered result.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Needs access to: puppeteer-core (an npm install into .ambition/), driving the Chrome already installed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Mode:            build · answerer: you · reviewer: you (final), with checks run at each step\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n"]
