[974.392, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ You confirmed the new goal for the animation. It's now a portfolio showpiece that makes AI coding look\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  uncanny. Your original request still holds in full.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What I did:** I asked about purpose, what \"excellent\" means, and how we'll prove it. I also checked what's\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  on this machine: Chrome and Node are installed, but `puppeteer-core` isn't yet.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What came out of it:** \"Excellent\" has five parts:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The fluid looks real.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Playback is smooth everywhere.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The first second grabs attention.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The technique is on show.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - It has hidden layers worthy of a real artist.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The proof will be:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Frame sheets:** pictures of 12 frames across the loop, at desktop and phone sizes, next to the first\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  version.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Performance:** browser frame-time traces at normal speed and with the CPU slowed 4×.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Loop check:** a comparison showing the first and last frames of the 10-second loop are identical, so the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  restart can't be seen.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Your review** of the rendered result.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Change of course:** the target moved from \"a nice animation\" to \"a liquid-looking showpiece with hidden\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  artistic depth\". None of the original request was dropped.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The page hasn't changed in this step; a snapshot is saved in `.ambition/steps/2/`. Installing `puppeteer-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  core` is the first piece of work in the next step.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[974.505, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Step 3 of pushing the work further: Depth. Open your first message with this line on its own,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  exactly: `▸ Step 3/8 · Depth`. Write that line nowhere else.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +15 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1055.161, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 3/8 · Depth\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The four statements**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **What a top practitioner would do that you didn't ask for.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Spike behaviour:** Real ferrofluid is *black*. Its colour comes from what it reflects. A master would\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  make the fluid a black mirror held up to a fauvist room, so the orange and violet arrive through reflection,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  not paint. Spikes would ride *with* their magnet in a lattice anchored to it, instead of blinking on and off\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  over a fixed world grid. Each pull would have animator's timing: anticipation, a snap with overshoot,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  capillary ripples and a settle.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Zoetrope:** they'd treat it as an optical device. The slits sweep continuously at 60 fps on the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  compositor while the images step at 12 fps.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Safety:** they'd also handle photosensitive safety and reduced motion, because a 12 Hz flicker is a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  seizure risk.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **The rawest material.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Physics:** Rosensweig (normal-field) instability, where spikes appear above a critical field and grow\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  roughly with √(H−Hc). Tip shapes are concave cones on a raised mound, and the spike pattern forms around the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  magnet.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Optics:** Schlick Fresnel for an oily dielectric.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Painting:** Matisse's *Open Window, Collioure* (1905), which reflects in the fluid as a hidden\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  homage. The fauves treated black as ultramarine-violet, and Van Gogh and Derain laid directional\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  brushstrokes along form.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Device:** the zoetrope's real slit-and-drum geometry.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Methods and instruments.**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Shading:** per-pixel analytic normals in the fragment shader so tips stay razor-sharp, a procedural\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  environment for reflections, smooth-max blending of per-magnet lattices, and closed-form periodic beat\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  envelopes so the loop is exact.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Animation:** a spring for the pointer magnet, and a CSS-compositor animation for the slits.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - **Measurement:** headless Chrome driven by `puppeteer-core`, with a deterministic `?capture` hook,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  contact sheets, an in-page pixel diff, and render timing under 4× CPU throttle.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **What proves it, other than me.** Rendered contact sheets beside the first version, a pixel-diff number\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  for loop frame 0 against frame 120 after a full run of the loop, and measured frame times.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The task, rewritten:** turn the fluid into a reflective black-violet liquid mirroring a fauvist room.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Spikes:** lattices anchored to each magnet; pulls with anticipation, overshoot and ripples; per-pixel\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  normals for liquid highlights.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Zoetrope and safety:** slits on the compositor at 60 fps with images stepping at 12 fps; flashes kept\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  photosensitive-safe; reduced motion respected.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Reveal and testing:** an optional field overlay (the \"technique on show\"), and a deterministic capture\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  hook for testing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Getting access first:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
