[2241.893, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I took the edge a portfolio scroller would want, a striking first second and a piece that answers the hand,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and built it from three borrowed methods plus fixes for what the red team found. The biggest visible change\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  is the camera: the pool is now a bright orange mirror with black spikes standing against it, where step 4\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  was mostly magenta.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What I borrowed**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Photographer's low, grazing camera:** the whole dish now sits in frame as a glowing orange ellipse on\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  violet, and each frame holds up as a still.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Zoetrope maker's crank-up:** on load the pool is a flat mirror with the magnets hovering high. The\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  images step in slowly (every 4th, then every 2nd) and the spikes erupt as the drum comes up to speed. After\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  about 1.8 s it is identical to the steady loop, and the loop is still pixel-exact.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Animator's smear:** each pull gets one stretched \"smear\" image on the snap, then a follow-through image.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Reduced motion turns this off.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Not taken:** the riso printmaker's two-ink misregistration, because it would compete with the liquid\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  look. Sound was also left out: browsers block autoplaying audio, and it would irritate people browsing a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  portfolio.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Red team fixes, all checked in Chrome**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Harm or break | Fix | Check |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | **Scroll trap:** embedded in a portfolio page, the piece swallowed all touch, so phone users couldn't\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  scroll past it | `touch-action: pan-y`: taps and sideways drags steer, vertical swipes scroll | Page and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  canvas both report `pan-y`, and a tap still steers. I didn't test a real swipe inside an iframe. |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | **Battery drain** while scrolled offscreen | It stops rendering when offscreen | Not exercised in the run\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Invisible to screen readers | The canvas is now an image with a description | Description is present |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | No keyboard focus on the button | Visible focus outline | Tab lands on \"reveal the field\" and the outline\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  shows |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Full test suite results**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Loop:** frame 30 matches frame 150 exactly, and the loop still returns to exact after the pointer is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  used.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Touch:** a tap changes 92k pixels.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Flashes:** the biggest brightness step is 0.052 against the 0.1 WCAG threshold, with 0 flashes. It's up\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  from 0.040 because the picture is now brighter.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Reduced motion:** still zeroes the flash and the shutter dip.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Draw time:** the typical draw is 5–12 ms at every size, and the 2560×1440 worst case dropped from 30 ms\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  to 21 ms. One outlier of 39 ms appeared on the phone size. These timings come from this machine's virtual\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  graphics chip, so they only stand in for real hardware.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Changes of direction**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The first low-angle render made ripples look like wood grain across the whole pool, even before any magnet\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  had engaged. Ripples now scale with magnet strength and are smaller.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The dish was cropped at the sides, so I pulled the camera back.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - On phones the dish still crops at the sides, which I kept because the spikes read larger.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  A snapshot of this version is in `.ambition/steps/5/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
