[3110.498, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I judged it with a test script instead of my own opinion: **the final version passes all 23 checks, twice in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a row; the first version passes 17**. The checks cover every part of your original request plus every\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  promise from the restated goal, run the same way on both versions.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Check | First version | Final |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Single page, three.js, no errors | pass | pass |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | 10 s loop seamless (frame 30 vs frame 150) | **fail**: 12 pixels differ | 0 pixels differ |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Loop really lasts 10 s, not shorter | pass | pass |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Zoetrope: image holds within a frame, changes between frames | pass | pass (0 pixels change within a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  frame, with the drum and shutter overlays hidden) |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Orange and violet in every frame (lowest share across 12 frames) | orange 5.4%, violet 6.7% | **orange\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  14.1%, violet 32.4%** |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Pointer response within one zoetrope frame | pass | pass |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Pressing pulls harder | pass | pass |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Loop exact again after interaction | pass | pass |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | A tap steers the magnet | **fail**: 0 pixels change | 90k pixels change |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | WCAG flash rule: at most 3 flashes per second | **fail**: 15 per second | 0 per second (biggest brightness\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  step 0.052, threshold 0.1) |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Reduced motion stops flicker and flashes | **fail**: opacity up to 0.619 | 0 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Draw time ≤ 16 ms, typical frame, 4 screen sizes | pass, 3–12 ms | pass, 4–12 ms (within 1–3 ms of first)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | \"Reveal the field\" (F) overlay | **fail**: doesn't exist | pass |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Phone layout at 390 px: no sideways scroll, no overlaps | pass | pass |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | On-screen text contrast ≥ 4.5:1 | 6.4:1 | 14.5:1 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Screen-reader description; vertical swipes still scroll | description **fail** | pass |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What the judge caught along the way**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A noisy test of my own:** draw time once failed at 1920 and 2560 after a text-only change, which can't\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  affect drawing. It was timing noise in this virtual machine. With 72 frames sampled instead of 24, the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  numbers are stable across repeated runs.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **A gap in the text:** a cold read found that phones showed no hint at all, so nothing told a phone\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  visitor they could tap. There's now a short phone hint: \"touch · you are the magnet\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **An unproven claim:** I'd claimed the within-frame change was only the drum moving. It's now proven, with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  0 pixels changing in the 3D image when the overlays are hidden.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The visual check:** all 12 desktop frames across the loop hold as stills. Each shows an orange mirror\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ellipse on violet with black spike clusters, and the arrangement changes from frame to frame.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Where it's weaker**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The phone view leaves the bottom third as empty pink-violet glow.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - On phones, the \"reveal the field\" button and the hint wrap onto two or three lines. Nothing overlaps, but\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  it's cramped.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The first version used slightly less GPU time per frame.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Draw times come from this machine's virtual graphics chip, so they only stand in for real hardware.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The acceptance test is `.ambition/tools/accept.js`, and `.ambition/tools/hold.js` checks that the image\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  holds within a frame. A snapshot of this version is in `.ambition/steps/6/`.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3110.64, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Step 7 of pushing the work further: Stretch. Open your first message with this line on its own,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  exactly: `▸ Step 7/8 · Stretch`. Write that line nowhere else.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +15 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3127.305, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 7/8 · Stretch\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Stretch target: draw each image in ≤ 4 ms (typical) and ≤ 6 ms (slow 10%) at 2560×1440 on a 2× display, at\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  *full* resolution with no 8 Mpx cap.** That's 14.7 Mpx in a quarter of the 16 ms budget, roughly 9× harder\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  than the current 12 ms at a capped 8 Mpx. It matters for this goal: a showpiece that stays crisp on a 5K\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  display with headroom to spare is the \"uncanny\" claim made measurable. The deadline is this step.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Fallback:** the current build, which already passes all 23 checks with the cap. If any attempt costs\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  visual quality or fails the acceptance test, it goes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **How it should be solvable:** demoscene shaders render far more complex fields at 4K. The usual tricks are\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  to stop paying for work twice and to profile before optimising. So first I'll find where the time actually\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  goes:\u001b[0m\r\n"]
