[3490.352, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ The ferrofluid animation is finished: still one page, `ferrofluid-zoetrope.html`, now with a 23-check test\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  suite beside it. The final passes all 23 checks; the first version passed 17.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **You asked for → it became**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **You asked for:** pointer-guided ferrofluid spikes in wild fauvist orange and violet, flickering through\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  zoetrope frames as magnets pull, as a 10-second looping three.js animation on a single web page.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **It became:** a portfolio showpiece meant to make viewers feel a human couldn't have hand-built it. It's\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  built to look like real fluid, stay smooth on big screens and phones, be safe to watch, and reward a second\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  look.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  How each part of the request was raised:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Ferrofluid spikes:** a black-violet liquid mirror. Spikes appear only past a field threshold, grow with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  field strength, ride along with their magnet, and form a hexagonal pattern with no seams between spikes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Pointer-guided:** the pointer is a magnet that responds within one frame. Pressing pulls harder and\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  sends out a ripple, a tap steers it on phones, and vertical swipes still scroll the page.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Wild fauvist orange and violet:** all colour is reflected from a painted room. The pool is an orange\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  mirror against a violet room, and a hidden nod to Matisse's *Open Window, Collioure* shows only in the sides\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  of the spikes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Flickering zoetrope frames:** the images step at 12 fps while the drum's slats sweep smoothly at 60 fps.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Flicker stays within the WCAG flash limits, and reduced-motion settings turn it off.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **As magnets pull:** each pull has anticipation, a snap with one stretched \"smear\" frame, overshoot,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ripples and a settle.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **10-second loop:** pixel-exact at the seam, including after someone has used the pointer.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Single page in three.js:** still one file, with a readable message if three.js or WebGL fails to load.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Against the first version**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Better on every part of the request:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - the loop seam is exact (0 pixels differ, against 12–94k);\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - tapping works (the first version ignored taps);\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - the flicker passes the photosensitive-safety test (the first failed at 15 flashes per second, against a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  limit of 3);\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - reduced motion is respected;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - orange and violet shares are 14% and 32% of every frame, against 5% and 7%;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - it reads as liquid instead of grass;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - the dish is fully in frame;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - it adds the field-reveal overlay (F), the crank-up entrance and a screen-reader description.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Given up:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - the first version's flat, bright salmon colour;\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - about 1–3 ms more GPU time per frame on small screens, though every size is still within budget.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Outside check:** `check/accept.js` drives headless Chrome on a virtual clock and runs 23 checks: loop\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  seam, real 10 s length, frames holding between steps, colour share, pointer, press, touch, flash safety,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  reduced motion, draw time at four sizes, the reveal, phone layout, text contrast, accessibility and scroll\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  behaviour.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The final passed 23/23, twice in a row. The first version passed 17/23.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - I also looked at a 12-frame contact sheet, phone frames, and 1:1 crops. Every desktop frame holds up as a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  still.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - One caveat: all timings come from this machine's virtual graphics chip, so they only stand in for real\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  hardware.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Stretch:** the target was drawing each image in ≤ 4 ms at full 5120×2880. It broke on the machine itself:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  even an empty frame at that size takes 5 ms here without anti-aliasing, and 10 ms with it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Kept:** dense displays now skip anti-aliasing and render at full resolution in about 11 ms. Before, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  capped 3771×2121 took 12–15 ms.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Rejected:** a faster per-pixel shortcut (8 ms), because the 1:1 crop showed harsher, stair-stepped\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  shading.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Bonus fix:** the stretch exposed seams at the spike bases, which are now fixed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Locked in**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `check/accept.js` and `check/package.json`: the acceptance test. Run `cd check && npm install && npm\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  test`; exit code 0 means all 23 passed. Add `--sheet out.png` for a contact sheet, and set `CHROME_PATH` if\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Chrome isn't in the default macOS location.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `CLAUDE.md`: how to run the check, which checks must keep passing, and a reminder to look at the contact\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  sheet.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - `.claude/commands/ferrofluid-check.md`: a `/ferrofluid-check` command that runs the test and reviews the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  sheet.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions made:** none. You answered every question.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Decisions**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **Real-hardware check.** Owner: you, by 2026-11-20.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - (a) Run the check on a real laptop plus one recent phone. *For:* the only check that isn't a stand-in.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  *Against:* about 15 minutes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - (b) Trust the virtual-chip numbers. *Against:* the real GPU cost hasn't been measured.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - I'd pick (a).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Glitter on far spikes.** Next check owned by me, by 2026-11-27.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - (a) Leave it. *For:* it's subtle. *Against:* it's visible in 1:1 crops.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - (b) Soften the highlight where spikes get smaller than a pixel. *For:* the standard fix, cheap.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  *Against:* it slightly dulls the far tips.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - (c) Render at higher resolution and scale down. *Against:* costs about 2× the GPU time.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - I'd pick (b).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Phone composition** (empty bottom third, wrapping text along the bottom). Owner: you, by 2026-11-27.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - (a) A dedicated portrait camera that is lower and closer. *For:* fills the screen. *Against:* one more\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  layout to check.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - (b) Leave it. *For:* nothing overlaps.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - I'd pick (a).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  4. **Where it lives.** Owner: you, by 2026-11-20.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - (a) Your portfolio host, embedded in a page. *For:* where your audience is; scrolling past it already\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  works.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - (b) A private claude.ai page link. *For:* shareable today. *Against:* not your domain.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - I'd pick (a), with (b) as a preview.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  5. **How three.js loads.** Owner: you, by 2026-11-20.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - (a) Keep loading it from the CDN. *For:* a tiny file. *Against:* depends on a third party, though it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  now shows a clear message if loading fails.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - (b) Put three.js inside the file, about 600 KB. *For:* works offline and forever. *Against:* a heavier\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  page.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - I'd pick (a).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Metrics**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Metrics since 2026-11-13T14:06:05Z (cost: /cost, or total_cost_usd in headless JSON)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  total   in 148 · out 123.7k (think 53.9k) · cache read 9.92M · write 183.3k · hit 98% · 74 calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  model   opus-5-5: in 148 · out 123.7k (think 53.9k) · cache read 9.92M · write 183.3k · hit 98% · 74 calls\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n"]
